+# DL-EXP-002 · Physical Manipulation Comparison
+
+Revision 1. Registered specification only, starting from PI02-P1. Reserve scenario IDs `dl-exp-002.tether-pulse`, `dl-exp-002.directed-launch`, and `dl-exp-002.garden-placement` for future loadable definitions.
+
+| Panel | Production input and required witnesses |
+| --- | --- |
+| Ordinary tethered Pulse | LT+A or Q+E acquires an eligible grain through the native owner. Charge and release ordinary Pulse while held. Observe native Pulse ID, accepted tether displacement and held identity. Treat later deliberate release separately. |
+| Directed material launch | Match the first setup and charge. Commit A/E while holding Stabilize and charging. Observe one directed release, aim/velocity, one reserve envelope and suppression of the second native Pulse. Report actual recipient only if confirmed. |
+| Controlled Garden placement | Start in the existing Garden catchment or traverse to it with the same grain generation. Acquire naturally, use held contact, brace and imprint qualification, and press A/E. Observe native seat and custody transition, separately from any accepted B1 ecological arrival. |
+
+Match underlying chemistry, Core configuration, pre-grip reserve, grain ID/generation/phase, finite census, environment, camera and input profile where possible. A/B share starting geometry. C must be at the Garden contact patch. Record exact staged differences and route/geometry eligibility. Test production input, accepted motion, release vector, charge, reserve, tether, placement acceptance and visibility. Record ledger and progression deltas and missed actions. Proposed three-panel 60–120 seconds with aligned start/charge cues and actual elapsed, individual source clips, optional future human takeover and raw telemetry. Chord comfort, visibility, distinction from tether Pulse, weight/momentum and retrieval require human evidence.
