+# DL02-C1 / DL03–05 · Director execution and capture
+
+DL-EXP-001 uses the admitted Silt Shelf with identical native material and patch, camera, reserve, chemistry stock and earned development. The same debug-prepared piece identities populate three layouts. Only the organization differs. Fixture staging occurs once, before the tape. Live input reaches the normal InputSystem and production owners.
+
+- Same input: latch Stabilize, start constant analog Flow at nominal simulation 0.45 s, and hold 2.2 s. Log actual edge/substep timing and partition variability.
+- Same objective: common selection, same demand and stop after 0.12 pressure·seconds or a common 3.8 s hold cap. Keep overshoot and real completion times.
+- In both: release, observe 1.3 s recovery and log position, action, reserve, strain, accepted receiver delivery and imprint, elapsed/deferred timing, and stable accounting. Report states that were attempted but rejected.
+- Capture: six original browser WebMs. Compose using source video start/end cue detection and wall-time anchors with an explicit elapsed axis, independent of gameplay timing. Preserve the source endings. Report anchor brackets, processing drift, decode metrics, and actual recorder limitations. The Playwright recorder produces silent video and offers no exact source-drop counter.
+
+Use `run.mjs <new-external-dir> --all` then `compose.mjs <run-dir> <new-output-dir>` after all acceptance conditions pass. Preserve individual source clips. Phone readability and physical-controller judgment are separate from geometric frustum evidence.
