+# DS02-C1 · Scenario contract v1
+
+PI02-P1 is the compatible checkpoint. `BLOB_BOT_SERIES1/director/scenario-contract.mjs` validates revision, provenance, exact Host/cell and Shelf receiver, basis and pose, Core placement/reserve, native material IDs/custody/generation, and fresh progression and receipt conditions. It validates neutral relationship state, camera and explicit existing experimental input profile. Null seed means no controlled random draw was supplied. Strict validation rejects unknown fields, arbitrary recipes, mismatched configuration, wrong build, and derived values offered in place of owner state.
+
+- Authoritative facts: initial placement inputs, reserve, owner membership, identity and prior progression. `shelf-stage.mjs` stages only documented placement, pose and reserve after the existing Shift+6 test mount and anatomy preparation. Real owner publications verify prerequisites and recompute derived traits and chemistry.
+- Presentation fields: explicit view/pitch/yaw/viewport. Transient input: neutral device, then existing normalized standard-pad profile. They carry no progression.
+- Protocol: named initializer, duration, required actions, acceptance predicates, telemetry coverage and fresh disposable reset. Track separate PASS, FAIL, NOT_EXERCISED, INVALID_SETUP and INCOMPATIBLE_BUILD outcomes.
+- Isolation: one new Playwright context per episode at an isolated Vite origin, native diagnostic telemetry limited to that context, ordinary context sentinel retained separately. Human handoff can use `run.mjs <new-external-output-dir> --prepare deep` when installed browser rendering is available. The prepared browser passes device controls through after start verification.
